{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015f7hABixCBmWDUw3bpJrD4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Docker Build Cache Explanation\n\n**How layers are cached:**\n\"Each instruction in this Dockerfile translates to a layer in your final image.\"\n\n**What invalidates cache:**\n\"Whenever a layer changes, that layer will need to be re-built.\" For example, modifying `main.c` means \"the `COPY` command will have to run again.\"\n\n**Downstream invalidation:**\n\"If a layer changes, all other layers that come after it are also affected.\" The document explicitly states: \"Once a layer changes, then all downstream layers need to be rebuilt as well.\"\n\n**Note on ordering guidance:**\nThe provided content does not include specific instructions about ordering Dockerfile commands to maximize cache reuse. The page references related resources on \"Optimize build cache\" and \"Cache invalidation,\" but those details are not included in the excerpt above."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","uuid":"551a8e75-1ee7-4ee4-a568-423be683f4fd","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:59:01.722Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":1897,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Docker Build Cache Explanation\n\n**How layers are cached:**\n\"Each instruction in this Dockerfile translates to a layer in your final image.\"\n\n**What invalidates cache:**\n\"Whenever a layer changes, that layer will need to be re-built.\" For example, modifying `main.c` means \"the `COPY` command will have to run again.\"\n\n**Downstream invalidation:**\n\"If a layer changes, all other layers that come after it are also affected.\" The document explicitly states: \"Once a layer changes, then all downstream layers need to be rebuilt as well.\"\n\n**Note on ordering guidance:**\nThe provided content does not include specific instructions about ordering Dockerfile commands to maximize cache reuse. The page references related resources on \"Optimize build cache\" and \"Cache invalidation,\" but those details are not included in the excerpt above.","durationMs":2821,"url":"https://docs.docker.com/build/cache/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KSeGip9qCECBao2BeX2chq","type":"tool_result","content":"# OCI Image Manifest: Definition and Key Components\n\n## Stated Goals\n\nThe specification aims to achieve three objectives:\n\n1. \"content-addressable images, by supporting an image model where the image's configuration can be hashed to generate a unique ID for the image and its components\"\n\n2. Enable multi-architecture images through a \"fat manifest\" which references platform-specific image manifests\n\n3. Ensure the manifest is \"translatable to the OCI Runtime Specification\"\n\n## Required Fields\n\nThe manifest includes four mandatory properties:\n\n- **schemaVersion**: \"This REQUIRED property specifies the image manifest schema version. For this version of the specification, this MUST be `2`\"\n\n- **config**: \"This REQUIRED property references a configuration object for a container, by digest\"\n\n- **layers**: \"Each item in the array MUST be a descriptor\"\n\n- **mediaType**: Should contain \"the media type `application/vnd.oci.image.manifest.v1+json`\"\n\n## Layers Array\n\nThe layers constitute the image's filesystem structure. According to the specification: \"The final filesystem layout MUST match the result of applying the layers to an empty directory.\" Additionally, \"The array MUST have the base layer at index 0. Subsequent layers MUST then follow in stack order.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","uuid":"2aa79deb-84dc-49af-a596-e25f92102f78","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:59:01.911Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":14008,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# OCI Image Manifest: Definition and Key Components\n\n## Stated Goals\n\nThe specification aims to achieve three objectives:\n\n1. \"content-addressable images, by supporting an image model where the image's configuration can be hashed to generate a unique ID for the image and its components\"\n\n2. Enable multi-architecture images through a \"fat manifest\" which references platform-specific image manifests\n\n3. Ensure the manifest is \"translatable to the OCI Runtime Specification\"\n\n## Required Fields\n\nThe manifest includes four mandatory properties:\n\n- **schemaVersion**: \"This REQUIRED property specifies the image manifest schema version. For this version of the specification, this MUST be `2`\"\n\n- **config**: \"This REQUIRED property references a configuration object for a container, by digest\"\n\n- **layers**: \"Each item in the array MUST be a descriptor\"\n\n- **mediaType**: Should contain \"the media type `application/vnd.oci.image.manifest.v1+json`\"\n\n## Layers Array\n\nThe layers constitute the image's filesystem structure. According to the specification: \"The final filesystem layout MUST match the result of applying the layers to an empty directory.\" Additionally, \"The array MUST have the base layer at index 0. Subsequent layers MUST then follow in stack order.\"","durationMs":4424,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opencontainers/image-spec/main/manifest.md"}}
