{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"message_stop"},"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"2546c26e-ee24-4199-a5b4-24f50d1a74cd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014dfDpEYTPjzsSNiSV2rd1N","type":"tool_result","content":"# OCI Runtime Specification: Filesystem Bundle\n\n## Definition\n\nA filesystem bundle is described as **\"a set of files organized in a certain way, and containing all the necessary data and metadata for any compliant runtime to perform all standard operations against it.\"**\n\n## Required Contents\n\nA Standard Container bundle must include:\n\n1. **config.json**: **\"contains configuration data. This REQUIRED file MUST reside in the root of the bundle directory and MUST be named `config.json`.\"**\n\n2. **Root filesystem**: the directory referenced by `root.path` in config.json, when that property is set.\n\n## Storage Structure\n\nThe specification notes that **\"while these artifacts MUST all be present in a single directory on the local filesystem, that directory itself is not part of the bundle.\"** This means a tar archive of a bundle should have these items at the archive root, not nested within a top-level directory."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","uuid":"2f801931-a653-4f07-bd98-059e51fc0468","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:59:54.417Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":1510,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# OCI Runtime Specification: Filesystem Bundle\n\n## Definition\n\nA filesystem bundle is described as **\"a set of files organized in a certain way, and containing all the necessary data and metadata for any compliant runtime to perform all standard operations against it.\"**\n\n## Required Contents\n\nA Standard Container bundle must include:\n\n1. **config.json**: **\"contains configuration data. This REQUIRED file MUST reside in the root of the bundle directory and MUST be named `config.json`.\"**\n\n2. **Root filesystem**: the directory referenced by `root.path` in config.json, when that property is set.\n\n## Storage Structure\n\nThe specification notes that **\"while these artifacts MUST all be present in a single directory on the local filesystem, that directory itself is not part of the bundle.\"** This means a tar archive of a bundle should have these items at the archive root, not nested within a top-level directory.","durationMs":2450,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opencontainers/runtime-spec/main/bundle.md"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HRDce5DbujeuAst7Jfje2i","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CNCF cloud native glossary container definition kernel\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Containers | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/container/\"},{\"title\":\"eBPF | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/ebpf/\"},{\"title\":\"Kubernetes | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/kubernetes/\"},{\"title\":\"Cloud Native Technology | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/cloud-native-tech/\"},{\"title\":\"Style Guide | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/style-guide/\"},{\"title\":\"Containerization | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/containerization/\"},{\"title\":\"Cloud Native Storage | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/cloud-native-storage/\"},{\"title\":\"Service Mesh | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/service-mesh/\"},{\"title\":\"Cloud Native Apps | Cloud Native Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://glossary.cncf.io/cloud-native-apps/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information from the CNCF Cloud Native Glossary about containers and their relationship to the kernel:\n\n## Container Definition\n\nA container is a running process with resource and capability constraints managed by a computer's operating system. The files available to the container process are packaged as a container image.\n\n## Containers and the Kernel\n\nContainers run adjacent to each other on the same machine, but typically the operating system prevents the separate container processes from interacting with each other. This is an important distinction from virtual machines—containers share the same operating system and its machine resources, spreading the operating system's resource overhead and creating efficient use of the physical machine.\n\nThe search results also show that kernel features are used in cloud native technologies. For example, a sidecarless service mesh design moves mesh functionality to the operating system level by using kernel features like eBPF.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","uuid":"23690d71-6c85-438d-bd39-4ed1c23a4aa0","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:59:55.291Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CNCF cloud native glossary container definition kernel","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XcKLiH3Pg5tphsUVj4kQyg","content":[{"title":"Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/"},{"title":"Containers | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/container/"},{"title":"eBPF | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/ebpf/"},{"title":"Kubernetes | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/kubernetes/"},{"title":"Cloud Native Technology | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/cloud-native-tech/"},{"title":"Style Guide | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/style-guide/"},{"title":"Containerization | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/containerization/"},{"title":"Cloud Native Storage | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/cloud-native-storage/"},{"title":"Service Mesh | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/service-mesh/"},{"title":"Cloud Native Apps | Cloud Native Glossary","url":"https://glossary.cncf.io/cloud-native-apps/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information from the CNCF Cloud Native Glossary about containers and their relationship to the kernel:\n\n## Container Definition\n\nA container is a running process with resource and capability constraints managed by a computer's operating system. The files available to the container process are packaged as a container image.\n\n## Containers and the Kernel\n\nContainers run adjacent to each other on the same machine, but typically the operating system prevents the separate container processes from interacting with each other. This is an important distinction from virtual machines—containers share the same operating system and its machine resources, spreading the operating system's resource overhead and creating efficient use of the physical machine.\n\nThe search results also show that kernel features are used in cloud native technologies. For example, a sidecarless service mesh design moves mesh functionality to the operating system level by using kernel features like eBPF."],"durationSeconds":5.188902800000011,"searchCount":1}}
