{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T2t3NJbSVE8zdCowA7sxS7","type":"tool_result","content":"# Docker's Definition of Containers and Comparison to VMs\n\n**Definition of a Container:**\n\n\"Containers are isolated processes for each of your app's components.\"\n\n**Key Characteristic - What Containers Share:**\n\n\"If you run multiple containers, they all share the same kernel, allowing you to run more applications on less infrastructure.\"\n\n**Definition of Virtual Machines:**\n\n\"A VM is an entire operating system with its own kernel, hardware drivers, programs, and applications.\"\n\n**Contrast Between the Two:**\n\n\"Spinning up a VM only to isolate a single application is a lot of overhead. A container is simply an isolated process with all of the files it needs to run.\"\n\nThe critical distinction Docker emphasizes: containers share the host's kernel, whereas VMs include their own complete operating system with a separate kernel."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","uuid":"f56cf91f-0c0e-4cc9-816d-bf4ea7b72063","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:00:25.174Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":8914,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Docker's Definition of Containers and Comparison to VMs\n\n**Definition of a Container:**\n\n\"Containers are isolated processes for each of your app's components.\"\n\n**Key Characteristic - What Containers Share:**\n\n\"If you run multiple containers, they all share the same kernel, allowing you to run more applications on less infrastructure.\"\n\n**Definition of Virtual Machines:**\n\n\"A VM is an entire operating system with its own kernel, hardware drivers, programs, and applications.\"\n\n**Contrast Between the Two:**\n\n\"Spinning up a VM only to isolate a single application is a lot of overhead. A container is simply an isolated process with all of the files it needs to run.\"\n\nThe critical distinction Docker emphasizes: containers share the host's kernel, whereas VMs include their own complete operating system with a separate kernel.","durationMs":3016,"url":"https://docs.docker.com/get-started/docker-concepts/the-basics/what-is-a-container/"}}
