{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AXuUtFkw9t8wn8cQcRAH5o","type":"tool_result","content":"# CRI-O Definition and Runtime Support\n\n**What is CRI-O:**\n\n\"CRI-O is an implementation of the Kubernetes CRI (Container Runtime Interface) to enable using OCI (Open Container Initiative) compatible runtimes.\"\n\n**Lightweight Alternative:**\n\n\"It is a lightweight alternative to using Docker as the runtime for kubernetes.\"\n\n**Runtime Flexibility:**\n\n\"It allows Kubernetes to use any OCI-compliant runtime as the container runtime for running pods.\"\n\n**Currently Supported Runtimes:**\n\n\"Today it supports runc and Kata Containers as the container runtimes but any OCI-conformant runtime can be plugged in principle.\"\n\n**Additional Context:**\n\n\"CRI-O supports OCI container images and can pull from any container registry.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","uuid":"4c8c760d-7844-45be-871e-83c4c9d460d5","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:00:51.676Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":19426,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CRI-O Definition and Runtime Support\n\n**What is CRI-O:**\n\n\"CRI-O is an implementation of the Kubernetes CRI (Container Runtime Interface) to enable using OCI (Open Container Initiative) compatible runtimes.\"\n\n**Lightweight Alternative:**\n\n\"It is a lightweight alternative to using Docker as the runtime for kubernetes.\"\n\n**Runtime Flexibility:**\n\n\"It allows Kubernetes to use any OCI-compliant runtime as the container runtime for running pods.\"\n\n**Currently Supported Runtimes:**\n\n\"Today it supports runc and Kata Containers as the container runtimes but any OCI-conformant runtime can be plugged in principle.\"\n\n**Additional Context:**\n\n\"CRI-O supports OCI container images and can pull from any container registry.\"","durationMs":3140,"url":"https://cri-o.io/"}}
