{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018kAjUApAtybf38Mhqq6gQ9","type":"tool_result","content":"# runc Description\n\nAccording to the web page, runc is defined as:\n\n> \"a CLI tool for spawning and running containers on Linux according to the OCI specification\"\n\nThe page does not contain any other verbatim statements specifically about runc's relationship to the OCI runtime specification or libcontainer."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","uuid":"e2d29361-e05a-461c-a51d-ab186bb25a59","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:00:53.485Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":14953,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# runc Description\n\nAccording to the web page, runc is defined as:\n\n> \"a CLI tool for spawning and running containers on Linux according to the OCI specification\"\n\nThe page does not contain any other verbatim statements specifically about runc's relationship to the OCI runtime specification or libcontainer.","durationMs":1387,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opencontainers/runc/main/README.md"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VGyzycQVNnKRL2xn6MGHZC","type":"tool_result","content":"# containerd Opening Description\n\n**Industry-Standard Container Runtime:**\n\"containerd is an industry-standard container runtime with an emphasis on simplicity, robustness, and portability.\"\n\n**Availability and Management Scope:**\n\"It is available as a daemon for Linux and Windows, which can manage the complete container lifecycle of its host system: image transfer and storage, container execution and supervision, low-level storage and network attachments, etc.\"\n\n**CNCF Status:**\n\"containerd is a member of CNCF with ['graduated'](https://landscape.cncf.io/?selected=containerd) status.\"\n\n**Runtime Dependencies:**\n\"Most interactions with the Linux and Windows container feature sets are handled via [runc](https://github.com/opencontainers/runc) and/or OS-specific libraries (e.g. [hcsshim](https://github.com/Microsoft/hcsshim) for Microsoft).\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89558532-ef37-43d4-ab5c-e8bf2bfb520f","uuid":"d4e9e6be-1c46-45a9-8747-17b3fe766365","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:00:54.456Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":11569,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# containerd Opening Description\n\n**Industry-Standard Container Runtime:**\n\"containerd is an industry-standard container runtime with an emphasis on simplicity, robustness, and portability.\"\n\n**Availability and Management Scope:**\n\"It is available as a daemon for Linux and Windows, which can manage the complete container lifecycle of its host system: image transfer and storage, container execution and supervision, low-level storage and network attachments, etc.\"\n\n**CNCF Status:**\n\"containerd is a member of CNCF with ['graduated'](https://landscape.cncf.io/?selected=containerd) status.\"\n\n**Runtime Dependencies:**\n\"Most interactions with the Linux and Windows container feature sets are handled via [runc](https://github.com/opencontainers/runc) and/or OS-specific libraries (e.g. [hcsshim](https://github.com/Microsoft/hcsshim) for Microsoft).\"","durationMs":3084,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/containerd/containerd/main/README.md"}}
